  "ingredients": [
    "0.25 cup garlic powder",
    "2 tablespoons seasoned salt",
    "2 tablespoons onion powder",
    "1 tablespoon dried oregano",
    "1 tablespoon salt",
    "1.5 teaspoons ground black pepper",
    "1 (12 fluid ounce) can light-flavored beer (such as Bud Light®)",
    "1 (3 pound) whole chicken",
    "4 green onions, sliced",
    "4 green onions, cut in half crosswise"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/uyD4nwRpXCwcp6yYrQjcC_6T2ZY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-step-1-1a28acb52692462babda249242b2f0bc.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine garlic powder, seasoned salt, onion powder, dried oregano, salt, and pepper in a small bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/txasAZSKBbDGMKZ1fGk8cQs0phE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-step-2-a883694b352640378959052c38d60cb9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour ⅓ first beer can into the bottom of a 9x13-inch baking dish. Place open beer can in the center of the baking dish.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/I3zjtqhlFgobSLX3GaLvOnbYdHU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-step-4-f8d9c65439f04e548fac50c147a946d6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rinse chicken under cold running water. Discard giblets and neck from chicken; drain and pat dry. Fit whole chicken over open beer can with the legs on the bottom.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/BJGvbXZILkuQBFvDv-UH78a6yiI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-step-4-1-d09cca88076f435e9ff0382b94d5c48b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut a small slit on each side of chicken breasts using a paring knife. Press the tip of each wing into the slit to encourage even cooking.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/31f4SsbSihhbT_Z8a4InaN34BPk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-step-5-762b4bd0f8974f8f9b85abad201b613b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rub reserved garlic seasoning mixture over chicken.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/b2jmwK6HCjhvKjaLKd_u6zc2ikA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-step-6-cfe81f0890494ed69b954a8a51b25ad6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pat green onion slices evenly onto chicken. Press green onion halves into top of chicken cavity. Pour ½ second beer can into the pan.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Ej-gisSGYlDxMeaqw9gtCocmoDM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-step-8-b6cda26d588c4f66a8dfbb47d624149f.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake chicken in the preheated oven for 45 minutes. Pour remaining beer into the pan under chicken: bake until no longer pink at the bone and the juices run clear, about 30 additional minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the thickest part of the thigh, near the bone, should read 180 degrees F (82 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/aZ3pE4WhXDDB2ndcav8o97_IOGs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-step-10-b7390091c33d4943aa84e8295878ac45.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_08.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Discard beer can. Cover chicken with a doubled sheet of aluminum foil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/9nS7Qiv8XxBgIHnA2Qipqy0ao3k=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-step-11-ea513e19e3c54290a78a61c23a921bd6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_09.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let rest for 10 minutes before slicing.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/uw5eERbMH3K3AwVcgNRDclwETaE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-214617-baked-beer-can-chicken-DDMFS-4x3-e9f8d03257c14d89922a47ce4d51635c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/214617/step_10.webp"
